== 3. three-ion Molmer-Sorensen GHZ at t = pi/(8 chi) (Section 9.6 row 2)
  x modes MHz [2.569, 2.8284, 3.0], eta of ions [[0.049, -0.0809, 0.0642], [-0.098, 0.0, 0.0642], [0.049, 0.0809, 0.0642]]
  global symmetric pulse: Omega/2pi = 151.67 kHz, tau = 50.0 us; closed-form pairwise chi {(0, 1): 0.7854, (0, 2): 0.8801, (1, 2): 0.7854} (COM only would be pi/4 on every pair)
    mode 3: |alpha|^2 (2n+1) = 1.10e-03, |chi| = 0.0196 rad, loop radius 0.036
    mode 4: |alpha|^2 (2n+1) = 5.85e-03, |chi| = 0.1535 rad, loop radius 0.081
    mode 5: |alpha|^2 (2n+1) = 6.10e-30, |chi| = 0.7462 rad, loop radius 0.487
  resolved [4, 5] at d_m = 12 (joint dimension 1152), frozen (0, 1, 2, 3, 6, 7, 8); frozen zigzag residual |alpha|^2 (2n+1) = 1.1e-03, chi = 0.0196 rad (the symmetric pulse closes the COM loop only)
  fidelity against the pairwise closed-form target: 0.98230
  fidelity against the ideal single-mode GHZ exp(-i pi/4 sum XX): 0.97346
  populations |000>, |111> = 0.2371, 0.0000 (the odd-N Molmer-Sorensen state has P(000) = 1/4, P(111) = 0 before the single-qubit rotation that makes it a GHZ state in the z basis); boundary populations {4: '1.3e-21', 5: '2.9e-09'}
  closed-form open-loop error of the resolved modes (the symmetric pulse closes only the COM): sum_i,m |alpha_im|^2 = 1.17e-02; carrier scale (Omega/nu_min)^2 = 3.49e-03; exact residual quanta {4: '1.15e-02', 5: '9.55e-05'}
  pair (0, 1): classes {3: 'resolved', 4: 'frozen', 5: 'resolved'}, frozen chi {4: 0.0}, spot check fidelity 0.99530, leakage 4.4e-03, dims [2, 2, 2, 10, 10]
  pair (1, 2): classes {3: 'resolved', 4: 'frozen', 5: 'resolved'}, frozen chi {4: -0.0}, spot check fidelity 0.99530, leakage 4.4e-03, dims [2, 2, 2, 10, 10]
